This dataset contains the DFT-labeled crystal structure prediction data used in the study “Accelerating Crystal Structure Prediction through Active Learning of a Foundation Interatomic Potential.”

The dataset includes relaxation-trajectory configurations generated from CALYPSO searches using the DPA3-OMat24 and DPA3-MP pretrained model branches for SiO2 and MgSiO3. For each DFT-labeled configuration, the dataset provides atomic structures, total energies, atomic forces, virial tensors when available, and the corresponding VASP calculation settings.

The data are organized by material system, pretrained model branch, pressure, and active-learning round. They support reproduction of the model fine-tuning, validation, candidate-ranking, and cross-pressure transferability analyses reported in the manuscript.

Main contents:

1. SiO2 CSP trajectory frames and DFT labels generated from the OMat24 branch.
2. SiO2 CSP trajectory frames and DFT labels generated from the MP branch, including data from the additional active-learning round.
3. MgSiO3 CSP trajectory frames and DFT labels generated from the OMat24 and MP branches.
4. Representative VASP INCAR files and calculation metadata.
5. Data mappings and directory information needed to associate trajectory frames with DFT calculations.

The dataset is intended for research on machine-learning interatomic potentials, crystal structure prediction, active learning, and high-pressure materials.